<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns">
  <key for="all" attr.name="label" attr.type="string" id="label" />
  <key for="all" attr.name="kind" attr.type="string" id="kind" />
  <key for="all" attr.name="status" attr.type="string" id="status" />
  <key for="all" attr.name="note" attr.type="string" id="note" />
  <key for="all" attr.name="arrays" attr.type="string" id="arrays" />
  <key for="all" attr.name="caps" attr.type="string" id="caps" />
  <key for="all" attr.name="read_ids" attr.type="string" id="read_ids" />
  <key for="all" attr.name="read_links_between_ends" attr.type="string" id="read_links_between_ends" />
  <graph id="JU1382" edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="I_5p">
      <data key="label">I 5′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">extended_open</data>
      <data key="note">Three HiFi molecules cross into the longer contig and two ONT reads anchored to I span the full 25.7 kb path. The near 849 bp graph cap has high depth and 102 C000005 molecules. Long apparent caps with strongest anchors elsewhere were rejected.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="I_3p">
      <data key="label">I 3′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">extended_open</data>
      <data key="note">The contig adds 27,663 bp. Three original ONT alignments span from I into the distal graph sequence. No confirmed distal telomeric tract.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="II_5p">
      <data key="label">II 5′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">germline_supported</data>
      <data key="note">Primary graph followed by an observed ONT allele with a 119 bp exact overlap. Several read molecules anchor in II; longer apparent caps include shared-repeat and wrong-arm matches.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="II_3p">
      <data key="label">II 3′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">extended_open</data>
      <data key="note">Multiple ONT reads independently anchored to II support about 33 kb of the contig; the last 7.3 kb of the graph candidate lacks this support. No confirmed distal telomeric tract.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="III_5p">
      <data key="label">III 5′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">germline_supported</data>
      <data key="note">The three graph exports give the same main path. Two ONT reads continue past it to terminal tracts. The selected source has a 49 bp exact graph-to-read splice.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="III_3p">
      <data key="label">III 3′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">germline_supported</data>
      <data key="note">A three-node low-depth path in both graph exports. Three ONT molecules align from III through the graph joins to its distal edge; one of them is a fold-back. Two continuous reads support the full route.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IV_5p">
      <data key="label">IV 5′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">provisional_distal_cap</data>
      <data key="note">The outward end of one double-telomeric HiFi molecule supplies +3,284 bp. Its IV anchor reaches the recorded inward cut at 5,066 bp. The longer apparent ONT cap group instead maps to V. The cap is provisional because there is one source molecule and competing repeat alignments.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IV_3p">
      <data key="label">IV 3′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">open_proximal_cap</data>
      <data key="note">The 6 bp repeat is an internal telomeric tract. Both graphs support a shorter capped branch. One HiFi read reaches the current tip 494 bp beyond the tract. Two ONT molecules independently join the tract to rDNA and end within the array. Germline cap assignment remains open.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V_5p">
      <data key="label">V 5′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">germline_supported</data>
      <data key="note">Identical primary and raw graph segment with a distal tract and a unique exact reference splice. Two C000047 HiFi and multiple anchored ONT molecules support the distal junction.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V_3p">
      <data key="label">V 3′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">germline_supported</data>
      <data key="note">An ONT molecule with 27 kb of V-facing alignment reaches a terminal tract. The selected splice preserves the graph through a 52 bp exact anchor. The distal repeat also matches II 5′ and alternative apparent cap reads anchor primarily there.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="X_5p">
      <data key="label">X 5′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">germline_supported</data>
      <data key="note">Identical cap sequence in both unitig graphs. Two original ONT molecules with the strongest long anchor on X 5′ reach this junction.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="X_3p">
      <data key="label">X 3′</data>
      <data key="kind">end</data>
      <data key="status">germline_supported</data>
      <data key="note">Identical 8.3 kb cap paths in both unitig graphs. HiFi and ONT match the graph junction; one ONT has a strong terminal X anchor and a farther split inward. Some longer ONT alleles show shared X-end repeats. Retained the graph representative.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="I5_short">
      <data key="label">I 5′ short cap</data>
      <data key="kind">graph route</data>
      <data key="status">alternative</data>
      <data key="note">High-depth p_utg/r_utg cap near the frozen tip. Continuations from I extend beyond its position.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="II3_far">
      <data key="label">II 3′ farther contig</data>
      <data key="kind">graph route</data>
      <data key="status">alternative</data>
      <data key="note">The last 7.3 kb of this contig path remain unsupported by whole-end molecules from II.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S01">
      <data key="label">S01 · 6 bp</data>
      <data key="kind">tandem marker group</data>
      <data key="caps">1</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="II3_far" target="S01">
      <data key="kind">local array</data>
      <data key="arrays">[(12863, 14135, 6)]</data>
    </edge>
